course: dictionary
lesson: 9563
title: Straighten: make it straight, tidy or fixed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To straighten something means to make it straight, or to become straight. Your arm can bend and straighten. A picture on the wall can be straightened with a little push. The same word has two other meanings in phrases.
explain: «Straighten up» means to stand up straight, or to tidy a place. «Straighten your back» means to sit or stand with a straight spine. «Straighten up your room» means tidy it, so the room is in order.
explain: «Straighten out» means to fix a problem or a misunderstanding. If two friends have had a quarrel, you can talk and straighten things out. The meaning is not about lines at all, so use the context to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Straighten is a verb: straighten, straightens, straightened, straightening.
fact: «Straighten» means to make something straight, or to become straight.
fact: «Straighten up» means to stand up straight, or to make a place tidy.
fact: «Straighten out» means to fix a problem or a misunderstanding.
fact: Muscles can only pull, not push, so they work in pairs: «the biceps bends the elbow and the triceps straightens it».
exercise: «Bend your arm and feel the biceps go hard; straighten it and the triceps pulls it down again.» What does straighten mean here? | *Make the arm straight | Bend the arm more | Hide the arm behind your back
exercise: Mum says, «Straighten up your room before dinner.» What does straighten up mean? | Make the room bigger | *Tidy the room | Paint the walls | Stand on your head
exercise: Two friends had a quarrel. Sam says, «Let's straighten things out.» What does straighten out mean? | Put the things on the shelf in a straight line | Ignore it forever | *Fix the problem by talking | Start a new quarrel
test:
«In cricket the bowler's arm mustn't straighten while bowling, so bowling is not throwing.» In this sentence, what does straighten mean? | Relax | *Become straight | Bend | Wave
«Muscles work in pairs: the biceps bends the elbow and the triceps straightens it.» Which muscle makes the elbow straight? | The biceps | *The triceps | The forearm | The umpire
exam: Which phrase means the same as «straighten up» when you talk about your posture? | *Stand up straight | Run away quickly | Shout loudly | Lie down flat
